Who We Are
Worldline helps businesses of all shapes and sizes to accelerate their growth journey - quickly, simply, and securely. We are the innovators at the heart of the payments technology industry, shaping how the world pays and gets paid. Our technology powers the growth of millions of businesses across 5 continents. And just as we help our customers accelerate their business, we are committed to helping our people accelerate their careers. Together, we shape the evolution
The opportunity
As the Legal Counsel, you will provide guidance, advice, and legal support to Worldline’s Financial Services and Merchant Services businesses in Southeast Asia and Greater China. You will collaborate closely with Sales, Project Management, Product, Executive Leadership, Compliance, and other internal departments to ensure alignment with local and the Group’s legal strategy and with applicable laws and regulations, with a strong focus on Greater China.
You will be part of the Northeast and Southeast Asia Legal Team. You will be based in Kuala Lumpur and report to the Deputy General Counsel. You will be part of a dynamic legal team within an international company and multi-cultural environment.
Day-to-day Responsibilities
Offer legal advice to business stakeholders with across a wide range of subject areas, including corporate, commercial, regulatory, employment and labor related contracts/matters/issues; data privacy; dispute resolutions/litigation management and legal compliance issues;
Draft, review and negotiate a variety of commercial agreements and documentation across Worldline’s payment and paytech ecosystem, encompassing sales, procurement, strategic partnerships, joint ventures, investments, and other innovative business models, addressing legal issues such as intellectual property, and data protection;
Provide legal advice on new business products and models, including Software, Hardware, Cloud, SaaS, AI, while staying updated on rules, regulations, and other statutory requirements;
Provide legal training and continuously creating awareness in the Worldline entities' in relation to Worldline’s policies;
Developing and maintaining contract templates;
Keeping up-to-date knowledge of contract law, new laws and regulatory requirements in various jurisdictions where we have a presence in Southeast Asia and Greater China;
Support corporate, M&A activities, including post-merger integration;
Instruct and liaise with external counsels as necessary;
Assist in initiatives to digitize the contracts archive and legal workflows, including contracts lifecycle management;
Apply effective legal risk management techniques and offer proactive advice on possible legal issues;
Communicate, manage and negotiate with internal stakeholders as well as external parties.
Who Are We Looking For
We look for big thinkers. People who can drive positive change, innovate, step up and show what's next – people with passion, can-do attitude and a hunger to learn and grow. In practice this means:
Required qualifications
Bachelor’s Degree in Law (LLB) from a recognized university;
Admitted as an Advocate & Solicitor of the High Court of Malaya or equivalent qualification;
At least 6+ years of experience in a reputable law firm or in an in-house legal department providing support to business in an international environment;
Experience working on Greater China legal matters and contracting;
Excellent command of written and spoken English, business-level proficiency in written and spoken Chinese and other Asian language;
Previous in-house technology agreements (software, hardware, platforms, cloud, networks) experience, and particularly payments sector experience;
Preferred Qualifications
Strong knowledge of and affinity with contract law;
Data privacy experience;
Demonstrable legal experience in the Asia-Pacific region
Proactive, responsive, team player, meticulous, hardworking, business savvy, high degree of flexibility in the organising of working time, excellent communications skills, good sense of humour;
Able to work in a fast-paced environment;
Enthusiastic team player who enjoys partnering with cross-functional teams to solve complex issues, invest in others, and work collaboratively.
Shape the evolution
We are on an exciting journey towards the next frontiers of payments technology, and we look for big thinkers, people with passion, can-do attitude and a hunger to learn and grow. Here you'll work with ambitious colleagues from around the world, take on unique challenges as a team, and make a real impact on the society. With an empowering culture, strong technology and extensive training opportunities, we help you accelerate your career - wherever you decide to go. Join our global team of 18,000 innovators and shape a tomorrow that is yours to own.
Learn more about life at Worldline at jobs.worldline.com

Responsibilities
Carry out the audit of the Group’s operating units including its wholly owned subsidiary companies;
Conduct follow up on all outstanding audit issues and recommendations to ensure that prompt implementation of agreed corrective measures by the auditees;
Assist in designing audit programmes for the execution of audit review and also to update the existing audit programmes to ensure high risk areas are adequately covered;
Prepare audit working papers with proper cross referencing, description of work done and supported with adequate evidence for each audit assignments to facilitate review;
Draft audit reports upon completion of every audit assignments with concise, factual presentation and able to write the audit issues in a proper audit report with minimum fundamental and grammar errors.
Assist in carrying out special review, investigation and other ad hoc assignments, as and when requested by the senior management and Audit Committee.
Requirements
Degree in Finance/Accounting/Business Administration or equivalent;
At least 3 years of working experience in related fields preferably from audit firms or oil palm plantation;
Good knowledge in Data Analysis;
Computer literate and proficient in Microsoft Office applications
Willing to travel within Malaysia and Indonesia;
Possess good interpersonal and communication skills and able to interact and communicate confidently with senior management;
Strong analytical and problem solving skills;
Highly independent and positive towards work commitments.
Prefably with working knowledge of audit software IDEA

Responsibilities
Perform structural and civil engineering design works with engineering principles and best practice;
Coordinate effectively with clients, architects, and other consultants to deliver comprehensive engineering proposal;
Attend site meetings with consultants and contractors to ensure quality project implementation;
Liaise with relevant local authorities to secure necessary approvals and clearances;
For Senior Civil & Structural Engineer, lead, mentor and oversee the team to ensure timely and high-quality project delivery.
Requirement
Bachelor’s / Master’s Degree in Civil and Structural Engineering, or equivalent professional
Responsible, committed, and possess a positive working attitude
Able to work independently with minimal supervision
Willing to travel within Malaysia when required
Fresh graduates are encouraged to apply
